                  %a{:href => "#joins_of_simplices"} Joins of simplices
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#simplicial_sphere"}
                    Simplicial
                    = succeed "-sphere" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#compatibility_with_quasicategories"} Compatibility with quasi-categories
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#compatibility_with_homotopy_coherent_nerve"} Compatibility with homotopy coherent nerve
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong join
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star T
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S, T
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            (
            %a{:href => "#Ehlers93"}> Ehlers 1993
            ) is a simplicial set that may geometrically be thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            with tip of shape
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            if both are placed in general position, cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+topological+spaces"} join of topological spaces
          %p
            The join operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            generalizes the historically earlier notion of join of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Spanier66"} Spanier 1966
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplicial+sets"} augmented simplicial sets
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#EhlersPorter00"}> Ehlers &amp; Porter 2000
            \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            If the simplicial sets in question are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+quasi-categories"} join of quasi-categories
            that underlies many constructions in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+in+quasi-categories"} limits in quasi-categories
          %h2#motivating_examples Motivating examples
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = \Delta^0
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star T
            is a genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = 2
            is the discrete two-point space, the join is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            For example, consider the two cones over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [2]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0]\star [2]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
