          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We first define the
            %strong join of simplicial sets
            as the restriction to simplicial sets of the extension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
            operation on the augmented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            to augmented simplicial sets.
          %p
            Then we give the more explicit definition in terms of concrete formulas. We first refer to the description of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplicial+sets"} augmented simplicial sets
          %h3#DayConvolution By Day convolution
          %p
            Via the general process of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+structure"} monoidal structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            is lifted to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+structure"} monoidal structure
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asSet"} asSet
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_+
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplicial+set"} augmented simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
            formula:
          .un_prop
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p The join of simplicial sets is equivalently expressed as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo +
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\star : sSet_+ \times sSet_+ \to sSet_+
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S \star S')(-)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\int^{[i],[j] \in \Delta_a}
                    (S_i \times S'_j) \times Hom_{\Delta_a}(-,[i] \boxplus [j])
                    \\,.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This is an abuse of notation because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\Delta_a}(-,[i] \boxplus [j])
              is a functor, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_i \times S'_j)
              is a set. To be precise, the second
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              should be replaced with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} indexed copower
          %p
            Note that the join of simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star T
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functor"} cocontinuous
            in each of its separate arguments
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (this is true generally of Day convolution products).
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              This join tensor product forms part of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal structure
              on the category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplicial+sets"} augmented simplicial sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asSet"} asSet
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi Sets
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi a
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coloneqq Sets^{\Delta_a^{op}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi asS
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ;
                    %msup
                      %mi Dec
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X, Y ]_n
                    \=
                    asS(X; Dec^{n+1}Y )
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Dec
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dec
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+d%C3%A9calage"} total décalage
              functor (see also at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/d%C3%A9calage"} décalage
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a simplicial set, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat S
              denote the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplicial+set"} augmented simplicial set
              which equals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in all degrees except in degree -1, where it is the point,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi pt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ({\hat S})_{-1} = pt
              %strong trivial augmentation
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong join
              of two ordinary
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_2
              is the join of their
              %em trivial augmentation
              \:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋆
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_1 \star S_2 \coloneqq {\hat S_1} \star {\hat S_2}
                    \\,.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Note that the join operation is not commutative. This comes from the fact that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+structure"} monoidal structure
              given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplex+category"} augmented simplex category
              is not
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmented+simplex+category"} augmented simplex category
              for more details.
          %h3#concrete_formulas Concrete formulas
          %p The join of two non-augmented simplicial sets is given by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi S
                  %mo ′
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∪
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (S \star S')_n \coloneqq S_n \cup S'_n \cup
                  (\cup_{i+j = n-1} S_i \times S'_j)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_i : (S \star T)_n \to (S \star T)_{n-1}
          %p
            is defined on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
            using the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in S_j
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau \in T_k
            , we have:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi i
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi τ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi j
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo −
                                %mi j
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mi τ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi i
                            %mo &gt;
                            %mi j
                            %mo ,
                            %mi k
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_i (\sigma, \tau) =
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  (d_i \sigma, \tau) &amp; if\; i \leq j , j \neq 0
                  \\\
                  (\sigma, d_{i-j-1} \tau) &amp; if\; i \gt j, k \neq 0
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j = 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_0(\sigma, \tau) = \tau \in T_{n-1} \subset (S \star T)_{n-1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_n(\sigma, \tau) = \sigma \in S_{n-1} \subset (S \star T)_{n-1}
                  \\,.
          %h3#join_of_quasicategories Join of quasi-categories
          %p
            If the simplicial sets in question are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+quasi-categories"} join of quasi-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over quasi-category
            construction.
          %p
            In this sense, the join can also be computed – up to equivalence of quasi-categories – as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy pushout
            of the two projections out of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times S'
          %p
            In this form, the join is used in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0608/0608040v4.pdf#page=42"} definition 1.2.8.1, p. 42
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
            Recall that the join of augmented simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star T
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functor"} cocontinuous functor
            in each of its separate arguments
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (this is true generally of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            products).
          %p
            This observation can help simplify calculations. For example, simplicial joins preserve unions in the first argument
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
          %p
            As an operation on simplicial sets,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star T
            merely commutes with connected colimits (since these preserve the property of having trivial augmentation). However, for each
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mo ∅
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cong S \star \varnothing \to S \star T
            induces a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star (-) : sSet \to S/sSet
            that does preserve colimits. Similarly,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \star T : sSet \to T/sSet
            preserves colimits.
          %h3#joins_with_the_point_cones Joins with the point: cones
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v\} = \Delta[0]
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %strong cone
            with cone vertex
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in sSet
            we say
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mo ◃
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\triangleleft \coloneqq \{v\} \star S
                is the
                %strong cone
                over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mo ▹
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\triangleright \coloneqq  S \star \{v\}
                is the
                %strong co-cone
                under
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Universal images of cones and cocones over a fixed base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limits and colimits in that quasi-category
          %p
            For instance, the cone over the interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
            is the 2-simplex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi v
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{v\} \star \Delta[1]
                  \=
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; v
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; 1
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\simeq
                  \\Delta[2]
                  \\,.
          %p
            More generally, the cone over the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            is the
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ◃
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[n]^{\triangleleft} \simeq \Delta[n+1]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Cones of 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"}> horn
            s are simplicial 2-squares
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq \Delta[1] \times \Delta[1]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi v
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mo ⇙
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[1] \times \Delta[1]
                  \\simeq
                  \\{v\} \star \Lambda_2[2]
                  \=
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  v &amp;\to&amp; 1
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;{}_{\swArrow}\searrow^{\swArrow}&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to&amp; 2
                  }
                  \\right)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mo ⇙
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi v
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[1] \times \Delta[1]
                  \\simeq
                  \\Lambda_0[2] \star \{v\}
                  \=
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  0&amp;\to&amp; 1
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;{}_{\swArrow}\searrow^{\swArrow}&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  2 &amp;\to&amp; v
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %h3#joins_of_simplices Joins of simplices
          %p
            Effectively by the definition from the ordinal sum, we have that the join of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            is another simplex:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mi l
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[k] \star \Delta[l] = \Delta[k + l + 1]
                  \\,.
          %p
            In particular, the cone over the
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[0] \star \Delta[n] = \Delta[n+1]
          %p and hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[n] = \Delta[0] \star \cdots \star \Delta[0]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that while
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n+1] \simeq  \Delta[0]\star\Delta[n] \simeq \Delta[n] \star \Delta[0]
            = succeed "-simplex," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial \Delta[n] \star \Delta[0] = \Lambda_{n+1}[n+1]
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[0] \star \partial \Delta[n] = \Lambda_0[n+1]
                  \\,.
          %h3#simplicial_sphere
            Simplicial
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[1] = \Delta[0] \sqcup \Delta[0]
            the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong simplicial 0-sphere
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta[1]
            with itself is a simplicial model for the
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}^0 \coloneqq \partial \Delta[1]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}^n \coloneqq \mathbf{S}^0 \star \mathbf{S}^{n-1}
          %p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}^n
            is equivalent to the topological
            = succeed "-sphere." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/9904/9904039v1.pdf#page=8"} Ehlers/Porter p. 8
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#compatibility_with_quasicategories Compatibility with quasi-categories
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S, S' \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              are both
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi S
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \star S'
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Andre Joyal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 1.2.8.3
          %h3#compatibility_with_homotopy_coherent_nerve Compatibility with homotopy coherent nerve
          %p
            There is also a join operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-categories"} sSet-categories
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D \in sSet Cat
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \star D
              to be the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Obj(C \star D) = Obj(C) \coprod Obj(D)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi D
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \star D(x,y) =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    C(x,y) &amp; for\; x,y \in C
                    \\\
                    D(x,y) &amp; for\; x,y \in D
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; for \;x \in D, y \in C
                    \\\
                    * &amp; for\; x \in C , y \in D
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p with the obvious composition operations.
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi hc
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_{hc} : sSet \to sSet Cat
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            functor (denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℭ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S, S'
              two
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the two inclusions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi hc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi hc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi hc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi S
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{hc}(S), \tau_{hc}(S') \to \tau_{hc}(S\star S')
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi hc
